    <!-- Field: /Page --></ix:exclude>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; color: Black"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

</ix:nonNumeric><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2023-01-01to2023-06-30" escape="true" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfRegulatoryAssetsAndLiabilitiesTextBlock"><p id="xdx_80F_eus-gaap--ScheduleOfRegulatoryAssetsAndLiabilitiesTextBlock_z5hQFJvijXT5" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; color: Black"><b>4.
<span><span id="xdx_829_zPF4b0mGdUle">ASSETS AND LIABILITIES HELD FOR SALE</span></span></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; color: Black"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; color: Black">On
June 13, 2023, the Company entered into a definitive agreement to sell all of its SaaS operating assets and liabilities to SW Sales
for $<span id="xdx_907_eus-gaap--ProceedsFromSaleOfProductiveAssets_pn3n3_c20230613__20230613_zg1PufOFpRqi" title="Sale of assets"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromSaleOfProductiveAssets" contextRef="From2023-06-132023-06-13" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">6,500</ix:nonFraction></span>,
including $<span id="xdx_906_ecustom--CashProceedsFromSaleOfProductiveAssets_pn3n3_c20230613__20230613_zIGUSxw5uXxk" title="Cash proceeds from sale of assets"><ix:nonFraction name="VERB:CashProceedsFromSaleOfProductiveAssets" contextRef="From2023-06-132023-06-13" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">4,750</ix:nonFraction></span>
of cash due upon closing. The operations of the SaaS business have been presented within discontinued operations. Upon completion of
the sale of assets to SW Sales, in which the buyer assumed all liabilities related to the SaaS business, the Company recorded an
impairment of $<span id="xdx_902_eus-gaap--AssetImpairmentCharges_pn3n3_c20230613__20230613_zMWUqaAXPIRj" title="Impairment charges"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:AssetImpairmentCharges" contextRef="From2023-06-132023-06-13" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">5,441</ix:nonFraction></span>
within loss from discontinued operations as the carrying amount of the net assets exceeded the sale price, less selling
costs.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; color: Black">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"></p>
